{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"The thresholds are **industry conventions, not universal SEC rules or safe harbors**:\n\n- **$0.01 per share** commonly serves as a de minimis/reporting-precision screen in NAV-error policies. Its exact operation depends on the policy and rounding methodology.\n- **0.5% of NAV (50 basis points)** commonly marks a material error warranting retrospective transaction review and potential reimbursement. Below-threshold errors are not automatically exempt from correction or compensation.\n\nCorrection is governed by applicable law—including Investment Company Act valuation/pricing requirements—the fund’s board-approved NAV-error policy, disclosures, contractual responsibilities, and the facts. Distinguish fixing the calculation from restating NAV, reprocessing transactions, and compensating the fund or affected transactors; these need not have identical triggers.\n\nFor ETFs, assess affected creation/redemption transactions separately from secondary-market trades: a NAV error does not automatically require repricing exchange trades. Neither threshold alone determines who bears losses."}}
